# PactFlow — environment variable template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env to version control.

# ─── Arc Studio internal variables (not needed outside Studio) ───────────────
# These are set automatically inside Arc Studio and have no effect when absent.
# Do not copy them to a standalone .env — the app does not read them.
#
# RPC_PROXY_BASE_URL=    (Studio-only RPC proxy)
# RPC_PROXY_TOKEN=       (Studio-only)
# RPC_PROXY_CHAINS=      (Studio-only)

# ─── No required variables for standalone hosting ────────────────────────────
# PactFlow uses injected browser wallets (MetaMask, etc.) and connects directly
# to the public Arc Testnet RPC (https://rpc.testnet.arc.io).
# No API keys, wallet private keys, or server credentials are needed.
#
# Contract and token addresses are public testnet values hardcoded in:
#   src/contracts/pactflow.ts
#   src/onchain-facts.ts
#
# If you extend this app with features that need a WalletConnect project ID:
# VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here
